---
/**
 * The admin's notification bell.
 *
 * **Deliberately the SAME bell as the site's, down to the class names** (owner, 2026-08-26:
 * *"שעובד באורך שלו ובמכניקה שלו בדיוק כמו זה של האתר הרגיל שבנינו"*). Every rule in
 * `styles/utilities/utils.css` — the dropdown's width and its 300px scroller, the unread tint, the
 * row's three lines, the fade-in — is written against `notif-dropdown`, `notif-item` and their
 * siblings. Reusing the markup means the admin's bell inherits all of it, including the parts
 * nobody would remember to copy, and a change to any of it moves both at once. A second stylesheet
 * for "the same thing, in the admin" is exactly the twin drift
 * (memory `project_brand_boost_twin_drift`) that this project keeps paying for.
 *
 * ── The two places it is deliberately NOT the same ───────────────────────────
 *
 * **No delete, and no "clear all".** The site's notifications are rows in a table, so removing one
 * is a real act with a real endpoint behind it. The admin's are DERIVED from the five sources that
 * put a number on a tab (`lib/admin-notifications.ts`) — there is nothing to delete, and a cross on
 * a row would either lie or invent a table to make itself true. What clears an item is opening the
 * tab it came from, which is the vocabulary the tab strip already uses. The head says so, once,
 * instead of offering a control that cannot work.
 *
 * **A click SWAPS a panel, it does not navigate.** The dashboard is one page whose tabs never
 * navigate, so `href` would be wrong here in a way it is not on the site; the target is carried as
 * a panel id and `scripts/admin/notifications.ts` hands it to `swapPanel`.
 *
 * Rendered inside the dashboard's own header row rather than in `Header.astro`: the site header on
 * this page is in `sellerMode`, which is what strips the cart, the wishlist and the account menu
 * from an admin session, and putting an admin-only control into the shared header would be the
 * first exception to that rule.
 */
---

<div class="notif-bell-wrap" style="position:relative">
  <button
    id="admin-notif-bell-btn"
    class="cart-btn"
    aria-label="התראות"
    aria-haspopup="true"
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="admin-notif-dropdown"
    style="position:relative"
  >
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 8A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 7-3 9-3 9h18s-3-2-3-9"/><path d="M13.73 21a2 2 0 0 1-3.46 0"/></svg>
    {/* Seeded EMPTY and filled by the first fetch, unlike the site's, which is server-rendered from
        a count the page already had. This page has the same five counts in hand — but they are the
        TAB badges, and seeding the bell from them would put a number on it a moment before the
        fetch replaces it with the same number, which is the badge flicker
        `project_injected_overlay_flash` is about in its other form. */}
    <span id="admin-notif-count-badge" class="cart-count cart-count--alert" hidden aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" aria-label="התראות שלא נקראו"></span>
  </button>

  {/* `--notif-clamp` is set by the script from the button's own position, so the panel can never
        run off the edge of the screen. Measured on the live demo before this existed: 340px wide,
        ending at 1626 on a 1440 viewport — nearly 200px of it unreachable. The site's own bell does
        not need this because it sits in a header whose end is the screen's end; this one sits
        wherever the header puts it. */}
    <div id="admin-notif-dropdown" class="notif-dropdown" hidden role="dialog" aria-label="התראות" style="max-width:calc(100vw - 1.5rem)">
    <div class="notif-panel-head">
      <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem">
        התראות
        <span id="admin-notif-loading-dot" class="dot-pulse" hidden aria-hidden="true"><span class="dot-pulse__dot"></span><span class="dot-pulse__dot"></span><span class="dot-pulse__dot"></span></span>
      </span>
      <button id="admin-notif-close-btn" class="notif-close-btn" type="button" aria-label="סגירה">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    {/* NOT "no notifications" (owner, 2026-08-27: *"ולמה הדרופדאון ריק?"*). The list is filled by
        a fetch, so before that answer arrives this element knows nothing — and a screen that says
        "there is nothing" while it is still asking is stating a fact it has not got. On a cold load
        that sentence is what a person reads and believes. The empty state is written by the script
        only once a response has actually come back. */}
    <div id="admin-notif-list" class="notif-list">
      <p class="notif-empty">טוען…</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
